   "id": "yehem",
   "title": "Three roads from Yehem",
   "time": "Spring, year 23",
   "narrative": "The army has marched north from Gaza and halted at Yehem below the Carmel hills. Scouts report three ways to Megiddo: a northern road by Yokneam, a southern road by Taanach, and the short road through the Aruna ravine, where men must go in single file. The generals urge a safe road. Thutmose reportedly reasons that the enemy expects exactly that, and chooses Aruna. The rebel coalition, gathered in and around Megiddo, has posted detachments on the two longer roads.",
