   "id": "aruna",
   "title": "Through the Aruna ravine",
   "time": "Days before the battle",
   "narrative": "Thutmose leads in person, with light infantry and mounted archers first to clear any pickets and the chariots and baggage strung out behind. The column is stretched thin along the narrow ravine for hours, and a determined enemy at its mouth could have destroyed it piecemeal. No one is there. The rebel main force is far off, watching the other two roads, and cannot reach the exit in time.",
